WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.823 --> 00:00:05.346
- [Narrator] The Mezquita has
always been a spiritual place,

00:00:05.346 --> 00:00:08.647
but has not always been
occupied by the same religion.

00:00:08.647 --> 00:00:10.806
Nowhere else in the world
will you find a cathedral

00:00:10.806 --> 00:00:13.723
built inside the walls of a mosque.

00:00:17.612 --> 00:00:20.847
Originally the site of a
temple to the Roman god Janus,

00:00:20.847 --> 00:00:22.695
the Mezquita was built as a mosque

00:00:22.695 --> 00:00:24.541
after Córdoba came under Moorish rule

00:00:24.541 --> 00:00:27.321
in the late seventh century.

00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:31.504
Then, in 1236, the city of
Córdoba came under Christian rule

00:00:31.504 --> 00:00:34.725
and the Mezquita was
converted to a church.

00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:36.281
Four centuries later,

00:00:36.281 --> 00:00:38.486
a cathedral was constructed in its center

00:00:38.486 --> 00:00:42.381
and it became a home for
the town's Roman Catholics.

00:00:42.381 --> 00:00:43.963
While the cathedral's an example

00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:46.563
of classic Catholic Baroque architecture,

00:00:46.563 --> 00:00:48.614
the majority of the
Mezquita's construction

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:52.281
is a result of the work
of Islamic architects.

00:00:52.281 --> 00:00:56.150
Features like 856 columns
and symmetrical arches

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.844
give the illusion of infinite space.

00:00:58.844 --> 00:01:01.072
These elements are examples
of why the Mezquita

00:01:01.072 --> 00:01:03.357
is considered one of the
greatest accomplishments

00:01:03.357 --> 00:01:06.135
in Islamic architecture in the world.

00:01:06.135 --> 00:01:09.176
Today, it is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.

00:01:09.176 --> 00:01:11.100
Over a million people visit every year

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.739
and after all its history,
it is now seen as a site

00:01:13.739 --> 00:01:17.906
of religious significance to
both Catholics and Muslims.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.310
(electronic chimes)

